// RUF041(n): a finding at node n, from clause `nested-literal`.
// Each rule below is one way the JSON `rule` can match.
.violation RUF041(at: node) "Flatten this nested `Literal` into one `Literal[...]` listing every value; if an inner group is reused, name it as an alias (`Mode = Literal[...]`) and nest the alias instead."
    suppress noqa "RUF041"
RUF041(n) :- ruf041_lit(n), ruf041_holds_lit(n), !ruf041_under_lit(n).

